.TH SDXI_VENDOR 3
.SH NAME
sdxi_vendor \- generic vendor-admin transport helpers for libsdxi
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <sdxi/vendor.h>

int sdxi_dev_admin_vendor_probe(sdxi_dev_t *dev,
                                const uint8_t guid[16],
                                uint32_t timeout_ms,
                                struct sdxi_admin_cpl *cpl_out);
int sdxi_dev_admin_vendor(sdxi_dev_t *dev,
                          const uint8_t guid[16], uint32_t op,
                          const void *in, size_t in_size,
                          void *out, size_t *out_bytes_inout,
                          uint32_t timeout_ms,
                          struct sdxi_admin_cpl *cpl_out);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The generic vendor-admin transport sends typed request and response payloads
through the driver's
.BR SDXI_ADMIN_VENDOR
path.
.PP
.BR sdxi_dev_admin_vendor_probe ()
uses operation
.B SDXI_ADMIN_VENDOR_PROBE
to test whether a vendor GUID has a registered handler.
.PP
.BR sdxi_dev_admin_vendor ()
uses size-in/size-out semantics for output buffers through
.I out_bytes_inout .
.PP
Typed vendor helper families live in explicit headers under
.BR sdxi/vendor/ ,
so the generic transport header remains vendor-neutral.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDXI (7),
.BR sdxi_dev (3),
.BR sdxi_dp (3)
